{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mr4dujpkkos","workspace":"/Users/imyu/Desktop/zonoid","title":"ls20 auto changing bar region and synthesis iteration lessons","summary":"Six live capture runs on ls20 (qwen-coding 36B, vision, fixed harness) produced a converging failure ladder, each layer removed by artifact evidence: extraction bugs -> token truncation -> wrong init_state contract -> numpy imports (whitelist drift between world_model loader and repl sandbox, now unified at 14 modules) -> UNKNOWN sentinel shadowing (models redefine UNKNOWN=-1; validator now aliases literal -1) -> synthesis starving gameplay (pacing interleave + per-game cap added). CURRENT blocker: ls20 has an auto-changing board region at rows 40-43 cols 34-38 (energy/progress bar repainting 3->12/9 after every action regardless of action); candidates repeatedly model it as static and fail validation on exactly those cells. Models cannot spot the changing region inside raw transition digit dumps; the harness must compute the auto-changing cell set from the TransitionSuite and state it explicitly in the synthesis prompt (or auto-mask). Remaining candidate-quality errors are small contract slips (step returning 1 value not (state, events)). All runs 0/7 levels so far; adoption is the next milestone. Artifacts under out/ewm-runs/ on orch/feature/arc-ewm-harness.","category":null,"tags":["arc-agi-3","ewm","ls20","iteration-findings"],"created_by":"main","valid_from":"2026-07-03T03:37:38.120Z","vec":[-0.09451743215322495,-0.052305642515420914,0.03357558697462082,-0.026643218472599983,0.08969248831272125,-0.009190371260046959,-0.0628831684589386,0.046260684728622437,-0.02197716198861599,-0.0005768862320110202,0.002093040384352207,-0.04801459610462189,-0.003515242598950863,-0.04151090607047081,-0.05326264724135399,0.03718302771449089,-0.015131328254938126,-0.049530308693647385,-0.05020638182759285,-0.03813882917165756,0.08767789602279663,-0.021408475935459137,-0.030792327597737312,0.011956115253269672,0.0